Best 55 (98.1%): instruction sequence is EXACTLY right, only register allocation differs (11 regalloc rows), so the source is found — only the allocator's choices are off. Working source (score 55):
  g = D_80111234; arg1[0]=0x020004E0; arg1[1]=0x2E0;
  p = g->unk30->unk4(arg0, arg1 + 2);   /* call through fn ptr at +4 of the struct at game+0x30, arg = arg1+8 */
  q = p; p += 2;
  q[0]=0x0C007FFF; q[1]=0x07C004E0; p[0]=0x0C007FFF; p[1]=0x09300650; return p + 2;
Layout/notes: the `g = D_80111234;` local is REQUIRED and must be the first statement (it produces the lui/lw at the top); `q = p; p += 2;` is required to get the extra `move a1,v1` + `addiu v1,v1,8` pair — writing p[0..3] gives `sw 8(v1)` instead, and `q = p+2` gets folded away. Do not reuse the arg1 parameter (that adds `move a3,a1`).
Target regs vs mine: target q=a1, 0x0C007FFF=a2, 0x07C004E0=a0, 0x09300650=a3; mine q=a3, c1=a0, c2=a1, c3=a2 (i.e. my constants grab a0/a1/a2 first and q is left with a3). Declaration-order swaps of p/q/g change nothing. Left to try: anything that makes q's live range look "first freed register" — e.g. an extra live-across-call temp, or a different expression for the call argument; or try another compiler flag (search_flags). Once this matches, func_800799E0 (needs=this one) uses the identical p/q idiom: q[0]=0x0D000000; p[0]=0x062E0000; p[1]=D_80111234->unk48; return p+2, and there target has q=a0.

Best 125 (39 insns, 38 mine). Fully understood: builds a 6-word display list and returns arg3+6.
sig: void *func_8007D960(u8 *arg0, u32 arg1, s32 arg2, u32 *arg3)
lo = arg1 & 0xFFFF; packed = (lo << 16) | ((arg2 * 2) & 0xFFFF);
arg3[0] = 0x08000000 | lo; arg3[1] = packed; arg3[2] = 0x0B000020;
arg3[3] = func_8007EAC0((s32)(arg0 + 8), (void *)packed);
arg3[4] = (*(u16 *)(arg0 + 2) | 0x0E000000) | (*(u8 *)(arg0 + 0x2F) << 16);
arg3[5] = func_8007EAC0(*(s32 *)(arg0 + 0x28));   <-- ONE argument (K&R call): ROM emits only `lw a0,0x28(s1)` in the jal delay slot with a1 untouched, so the original prototype at that site had no second param. context.h says (s32, void*) so I called through `((s32 (*)())func_8007EAC0)(...)` - keep that.
*(s32 *)(arg0 + 0x2C) = 0; return arg3 + 6;
Remaining diffs (best attempt): (a) arg3[4]: target groups as `v1 = lhu(2) ; a0 = 0x0E000000 ; or v1,v1,a0 ; v0 = lbu(0x2F)<<16 ; or v0,v0,v1`, gcc always reassociates the source tree to `(shift | 0x0E000000) | unk02` (tried both operand orders, and separate `high`/`low` variables - the variables fix the grouping but then the load order/regs and the prologue scheduling shift, score 515/520). (b) target ends `addiu s0,s0,0x18 ; move v0,s0`, gcc folds `arg3 += 6; return arg3;` into `addiu v0,s0,0x18`; the move did not appear in any variant.
Approach that scored 125/130 (start there): no temp for the low/high parts, plain `arg3[4] = ... | ...; ...; return arg3 + 6;`.

Best 300 (35 insns both, first 20 identical). Structure fully recovered (wrap + fabs):
f32 func_8007D9FC(UnkD9FC *arg0, s32 arg1) {   /* arg0 floats: +0x10, +0x14, +0x1C */
    f32 angle = arg0->unk14 + arg0->unk10 * (f32)arg1;  /* lwc1 unk10, mul.s, lwc1 unk14, add.s f2,f2,f0 */
    arg0->unk14 = angle;                                 /* store scheduled into the wrap-branch delay slot */
    if (angle > D_80115948 /*2.0*/) angle = angle - D_80115950 /*4.0*/;  /* double cmp/sub, cvt.s.d */
    arg0->unk14 = angle;
    return arg0->unk1C * (f32)((angle < 0.0f ? -angle : angle) - D_80115958 /*1.0*/);
}
Declare the constants as `extern f64 D_80115948/D_80115950/D_80115958` (literals would emit .rodata refs).
Only remaining diff is float-register allocation in the fabs block: target `mov.s f4,f2 ; c.lt.s f2,f0 ; bc1f ; swc1 f2,0x14(a0) ; neg.s f4,f2` then tail uses f2 for the result/double and f0 for the constant and unk1C. mine always `mov.s f4,f2 ; c.lt.s f4,f0 ; ... swc1 f4 ; neg.s f4,f4` with the tail mirrored (f0 value / f2 constant) -> gcc copy-propagates the `a = angle` copy into the compare. Tried: named temp + if, if/else, expression-level `?:` (all 300), store before/after the if, declaration orders (765/1060 when if/else or unk values go to f6). Plateau 300; next agent: get the compare to read the *original* angle register while keeping it live for the store (e.g. something gcc can't treat as a copy).

Matched (18 insns). Bump allocator: arg2 is {u32 unk0 (base/limit?), u32 unk4 (cur), u32 unk8 (size end?)}; args are (void *arg0 unused, void *arg1 unused, SAlloc *arg2, s32 count, s32 size) — the 5th argument arrives on the stack (lw v0,0x10(sp)). C that matches:
    u32 size = (arg3 * arg4 + 0xF) & ~0xF;
    u32 cur = arg2->unk4;
    u32 next = cur + size;
    u32 ret = 0;
    if (arg2->unk0 + arg2->unk8 >= next) { ret = cur; arg2->unk4 = next; }
