Declaring/computing `size` FIRST is what makes unk8 land in v1 and the -0x10 mask in a0 (score 95 otherwise, 270 if you reorder the declarations).

Best 145 (93%), 20/21 insns. Working source (for loop, produced the 0x8 frame!):
  s32 count; s32 i; u8 *p;
  count = D_802AC994; p = D_802AC99C;
  for (i = 0; i < count; i++) { if (*(s32*)(p+0x44) == arg0) *(s32*)p = (*(s32*)p & arg1) | arg2; p += 0x13C; }
(result type void; D_802AC99C is a u8* pointer variable, D_802AC994 an s32 count.)

Only remaining difference: TARGET loads D_802AC994 into $v0, does `blez v0,end; move a3,zero`, then `move t0,v0` (saves loop bound in t0 because v0 is clobbered by `lw v0,0x44(v1)` in the loop), loop compares `i < t0`. MINE: gcc allocates count straight to $t0 (`lui/lw t0`, `blez t0`) so the `move t0,v0` is missing (1 insn short). Tried: for vs while vs do-while (do-while loses the frame), use global in for-condition (reloads it each iteration), declaration orders. Not tried: making count come from an expression/field that gcc loads into v0 (a second use of count in v0, or `count > i` operand order), or a second local bound variable (if gcc does not coalesce). Everything else (frame, loop body, pointer walk) already matches. Note: the 0x8 frame appears exactly when using a for/while loop here.

This family (func_80078F10 / 791A0 / 79230 / 79370 / 79400) builds a command in the block from func_80079858(). Matched 79400/79370 prove the source order: the sum assignment comes FIRST, then the other stores in target address order. For 79400:

    p = func_80079858();
    if (p != NULL) {
        p->unk04 = D_80111234->unk1C + arg0->unk08->unk88;  /* FIRST */
        p->unk08 = 0xF;    /* sh */
        p->unk00 = 0;      /* sw */
        func_800776F8(arg0->unk08, 3, p);
    }

That gives the ROM's loads-then-stores schedule and v1/a0 registers. For 79370 add p->unk0C = arg1; then p->unk00 = 0; then p->unk0A = arg0->unk1A; all after the sum. So 79230 should be: p->unk04 = ...; p->unk08 = 7; p->unk0C = arg1 (swc1); p->unk00 = 0; then call.

Best attempt scores 216 (95.7%, 51/51 insns). Everything matches byte-for-byte except ONE ordering difference in the s16 test of the do-while condition.

Matched (do NOT change):
```c
void func_80068BC0(s32);
extern s32 D_803253A8[][16];
typedef struct S97Item { s32 flags; s32 unk4; } S97Item;
extern S97Item D_80097C94[2][16];

s32 func_80068DA0(u8 *arg0, s32 arg1) {   /* arg0: byte pointer (caller passes &D_803246E0) */
    s32 val;
    do {
        val = D_803253A8[arg1][0];
        func_80068BC0(arg1);
    } while ((D_80097C94[arg1][val].flags & 0x40) && (*(s16 *)(arg0 + arg1 * 2 + 0x4B0) != -1));
    return val;
}
```
- The loop MUST be `do { } while (A && B)` with two && terms: `while(1){if(!A)break;if(!B)break;}` gives the inverted branch layout and scores ~950. This form produces the exact `beqz`->exit / `bne`->loop layout.
- D_80097C94 must be `S97Item[2][16]` indexed `[arg1][val].flags` (8-byte entries): gives the exact `sll 3 / sll 7 / addu / lui+addu+lw %lo` sequence. Most other spellings (byte-offset expressions, [][1]/cast, S97Item[] with val+arg1*16) score 1037-2516.
- D_803253A8 must be `s32[][16]` and indexed `[arg1][0]` (stride 64).

Remaining diff (target vs best):
```
TARGET: lw v0,0x20(fp); lw v1,0x24(fp); move a0,v1; sll v1,a0,1; addu v0,v1,v0; addiu v1,v0,0x4b0; lh v0,0(v1)
YOURS : lw v0,0x24(fp); move v1,v0; sll v0,v1,1; lw v1,0x20(fp); addu v0,v0,v1; addiu v1,v0,0x4b0; lh v0,0(v1)
```
i.e. identical instructions, but the ROM evaluates the arg0 operand of `arg0 + arg1*2` BEFORE the `arg1*2` multiply; GCC 2.7.2 here canonicalises the commutative PLUS to put the MULT first and evaluates it first. Tried: arg0+arg1*2, arg1*2+arg0, (arg1<<1), u8*/s32/volatile u8* arg0 — all evaluate arg1*2 first (216->336 for the shift form). Untried ideas: make the arg0 term a more complex tree that folds ahead of the MULT (e.g. an &arg0[...] form) while keeping the final constant add AFTER the sum, or a struct/array type that makes GCC expand the base pointer first.

Best score 140 (58/58 insns, only block ordering + 2 operands). Best source:

typedef struct { s32 unk0; u8 pad[0x10]; } S51658Rec;
extern s32 D_80300210, D_80324E30; extern s8 D_80324B94; extern S51658Rec D_80324B40[];
s32 func_80051658(void){
    for(;;){
        D_80300210++;
        if (D_80300210 != D_80324E30) {
            if (!(D_80324B40[D_80300210].unk0 & 2)) continue;
            break;
        }
        if (D_80300210 >= D_80324B94) break;
    }
    if (D_80300210 < D_80324B94) return 1;
