Cannot get closer under the current project flags — the remaining diff is entirely the second scheduling pass. try_compiler proves the C below is byte-identical with -fno-schedule-insns2; under the current sched2-on flags it is 810. Open suggest() asks for -fno-schedule-insns2. Please release so the next agent/claim can proceed; when the flags are applied this function matches as given.

void *func_80089500(void *arg0, s32 arg1, u32 arg2) {
    u8 *p; u32 n; u32 c; s32 i;
    n = arg2;
    if (n == 0) return arg0;
    p = (u8 *)arg0;
    c = arg1 & 0xFF;
    c |= c << 8;
    c |= c << 16;
    if ((u32)p & 1) { *p++ = c; n--; }
    if (n >= 2) {
        if ((u32)p & 2) { *(u16 *)p = c; p += 2; n -= 2; }
    }
    i = n >> 2;
    while (--i != -1) { *(u32 *)p = c; p += 4; }
    if (n & 2) { *(u16 *)p = c; p += 2; }
    if (n & 1) *p = c;
    return arg0;
}
(memset; returns arg0; note `while (--i != -1)` for the ROM's beql sentinel loop.)

Single-bit mask trick: `return (*(volatile u32*)0xA410000C & 0x100) != 0;` gets rewritten by KMC GCC -O2 into `srl v0,8; andi v0,1` (score 270). Assigning the masked value to a local first makes GCC keep the AND and gives the ROM's `andi 0x100; sltu v0,zero,v0`:
```c
u32 v; u32 m;
v = *(volatile u32 *)0xA410000C;
m = v & 0x100;
return m != 0;
```
(Also `> 0`, `== 0x100`, u32/s32, operand swap, and every flag variant all gave the srl form. The magic is the intermediate variable.) Same trick: keep a comparison result in a local so `&` stays a register AND.

