Cannot get closer in a few compiles; remaining is register-copy shape only. Best source = 190 (reproduce it):
s32 func_800889A0(u16 *arg0, u16 *arg1) {
    u32 exp; s32 t; u16 v;
    v = arg1[0];
    exp = (v & 0x7FF0) >> 4;
    t = exp;
    if (t == 0x7FF) {
        arg0[0] = 0;
        if ((arg1[0] & 0xF) != 0 || arg1[1] != 0 || arg1[2] != 0 || arg1[3] != 0) return 2;
        return 1;
    }
    if (t > 0) {
        arg1[0] = (v & 0x800F) | 0x3FF0;
        arg0[0] = exp - 0x3FE;
        return -1;
    }
    if (t < 0) return 2;
    arg0[0] = 0;
    return 0;
}
ROM wants exp computed into a3, a copy in a2 used for the comparisons, and a copy of arg1 in t0 used for the positive-path store (`sh v1,0(t0)`); it also emits `move t0,a1` in the bne delay slot. Mine puts the computed value in a2, the copy in a3 (move a3,a2 in the delay), no t0. Tried swapping t/exp order, u32/s32 casts, and a separate `u16 *p = arg1` for the store (p coalesces, no t0) - all 190/385. Next: find the source shape that makes gcc allocate the long-lived exponent to a3 and the comparison copy to a2 (maybe compute the value into a signed local and copy into an unsigned one, or vice versa), and consider that t0 may come from arg1 being cast/used through a second type in the store. Check with -fno-schedule-insns2 (open suggest).

Best 270 (kept): 27/27 instructions, all semantics right; ONLY the prologue schedule differs, 2 rows reordered, no count/operand/regalloc difference. ROM: `addiu sp,-0x18; sw ra,0x14; sw s0,0x10; addiu v0,a2,-2; sltiu v0,0x23; bnez v0,.L80089204; addu s0,a1,zero (delay slot); j end; sb zero,0(s0)`. Mine: `addiu sp,-0x18; sw s0,0x10; move s0,a1; addiu v0,a2,-2; sltiu; bnez; sw ra,0x14 (delay); j end; sb zero,0(s0)`. So in the ROM reorg moves the arg1->s0 copy into the bnez delay slot and leaves both saves in the prologue; in mine the s0 copy stays before the condition and reorg sinks sw ra into the delay slot instead. Tried: early-return vs if/else; p=arg1 at entry vs inside the else; v=arg0 local vs using arg0 directly; condition block as then vs else - all identical 270. Declaration/expr order changes made it worse (560): declaring isTen before p and hoisting `isTen = (arg2 == 0xA);` moves the condition insns before the branch but keeps the s0 copy early. Next idea: force arg1's callee-saved copy later, e.g. return value expressed so the invalid-path store reads a1 directly, or a source that makes the s0 copy the last insn before the bnez.

Critical condition trick (needed, else 800-1270): keep the equality in a local so `&` stays a register AND:
```c
s8 *func_80089960(s32, s8 *);
s8 *func_800891E0(u32 arg0, s8 *arg1, s32 arg2) {
    s8 *p; s32 isTen;
    if ((u32)(arg2 - 2) >= 0x23) { *arg1 = 0; }
    else {
        p = arg1;
        isTen = (arg2 == 0xA);
        if (isTen & (arg0 >> 31)) { *arg1 = 0x2D; p = arg1 + 1; arg0 = -arg0; }
        *func_80089960(arg0, p) = 0;
    }
    return arg1;
}
```
Writing `(arg2 == 0xA) & (arg0 >> 31)` directly gets converted to && (bne/bgez branches).

