Not C — the loop bodies are MIPS `cache` instructions, which no compiler can emit from C.

Evidence: both loops' only body instruction is `cache 0x10,0($t0)` (index invalidate) and `cache 0x00,0($t0)` (index writeback invalidate). GCC 2.7.2 (KMC) has no `__builtin_cache`, no `__asm__`-free way to produce COP0 opcode 0x2F, and the disassembler itself tags both as "/* handwritten instruction */". Together with the literal `nop` delay slots throughout and the `sltu $at,...` compare-then-branch expansions, this is the hand-written libultra osInvalDCache / osWritebackDCache pair. Nothing in C can produce it, so no compile budget should be spent here.

