CRITICAL, and the reason my first bitfield attempt scored 10 with `srl $v0,$v1,0xe`: N64 is big-endian, so bitfields are allocated MSB-first — the FIRST declared field takes the unit's TOP bits. My wrong attempt declared `bit0:1; bit1:1; rest:14`, which puts that field at bit 14 (hence srl 14). To land on LSB position P in a 16-bit unit you must declare `15 - P` bits before it. For bit 1 that is 14 bits, as above.

